---
// Old /how-to-claim/ page, word for word apart from the FCA dates (Jack, 2 Nov 2026).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { SITE, PARTNER, FREE_ROUTE, PAYMENT_LINE, CLAIM_URL } from '../data/site';

const QUESTIONS = [
  'Did you enter into a Personal Contract Purchase (PCP) or Hire Purchase (HP) agreement?',
  'Did you take out your finance agreement between April 2007 and November 2024?',
  'Were you aware the broker or dealer would receive a commission for arranging your finance?',
  'Did you know they had the ability to set or adjust the interest rate on your agreement?',
  'Did you go through proper affordability checks?',
  'Were the terms of your agreement clearly explained to you?',
  'Did you feel pressured to agree on the deal?',
  'Were you presented with multiple financial packages?',
  'Were all the fees and charges explained to you upfront?',
  'Did you think you’d own your car after the PCP agreement?',
];
---
<Base path="/how-it-works/" title={`How It Works | ${SITE.name} | Car Finance Claims`} description={`If you believe you may have been mis-sold a car finance agreement, compensation could be just around the corner. ${SITE.name} can help you make a claim.`} active="how" crumbs={[{ name: 'How it works', href: '/how-it-works/' }]}>
  <PageHero slot="hero" h1="How to claim" lede={`If you believe you may have been mis-sold a car finance agreement, compensation could be just around the corner. ${SITE.name} can help you make a claim!`} crumbs={[{ name: 'How it works', href: '/how-it-works/' }]}>
    <div><a class="btn" href={CLAIM_URL} rel="sponsored noopener">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 class="d h2">Getting the right deal</h2>
      <p>Check whether you may be eligible for compensation for mis-sold car finance!</p>
    </div>
    <div class="know">
      <div><h3 class="h3">Loan size</h3><p>The larger the loan the more significant your payments, which may in turn affect potential compensation.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="h3">Length of agreement</h3><p>Longer agreements mean you may have paid more interest than you needed to.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="h3">Interest rates</h3><p>If the rate you were charged is higher than it should’ve been, your compensation could be higher too.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band-mint">
    <div class="wrap section two-col">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="d h2">Can I claim?</h2>
        <p class="muted">Sign up to assess your eligibility and get started!</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stack" style="gap:24px">
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><div class="rail"><i></i><u></u></div><div class="body"><h3 class="h3">Add your details</h3><p>Add your personal details like name, date of birth, address and sign up.</p></div></li>
          <li><div class="rail"><i></i><u></u></div><div class="body"><h3 class="h3">We look for your agreements</h3><p>We look for your finance agreements, tell you if you can claim.</p></div></li>
          <li><div class="rail"><i></i></div><div class="body"><h3 class="h3">You decide</h3><p>You decide if you would like our claims handling partner(s) to represent you.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
        <div><a class="btn" href={CLAIM_URL} rel="sponsored noopener">Find my agreements <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section two-col">
    <div class="stack">
      <h2 class="d h2">What happens next?</h2>
      <p class="muted">From confusion to conclusion</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose" style="gap:14px">
      <p>If you decide that you would like our partner ({PARTNER.name}) to represent you, you must agree and sign their terms and conditions, a confirmation email will be sent once you have done this.</p>
      <p>The Financial Conduct Authority has looked into mis-sold car finance, focusing on getting anyone who’s overpaid their money back, and has set up a redress scheme. Payouts under the scheme are on hold until a legal challenge is heard from 16 February to 3 March 2027. See <a href="/fca-redress-scheme/">the FCA scheme</a>.</p>
      <ol class="steps" style="margin-top:6px">
        <li><div class="rail"><i></i><u></u></div><div class="body"><h3 class="h3">Step 1</h3><p>Our partner, {PARTNER.name}, will contact your lender by letter to make a claim on your behalf.</p></div></li>
        <li><div class="rail"><i></i><u></u></div><div class="body"><h3 class="h3">Step 2</h3><p>The lender should reply or at least acknowledge your complaint.</p></div></li>
        <li><div class="rail"><i></i></div><div class="body"><h3 class="h3">Step 3</h3><p>Your lender must reply, but payouts under the FCA’s scheme are on hold until the legal challenge is decided.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="small muted">No win no fee: this means that a customer will typically pay 30% + VAT (36% including VAT) of any amount recovered by a Claims Management Company, although this will be subject to your individual circumstances and the actual fee may be less than this but it will never be more. A cancellation fee may be charged by a third party/Claims Management Company if you cancel outside the cooling off period. You do not need to use a claims management company to make a car finance claim; you can do this yourself for free by contacting the car dealership or finance provider and if that is not successful you can complain to the Financial Ombudsman Service. {PAYMENT_LINE}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band-mint">
    <div class="wrap section two-col">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="d h2">Questions to ask</h2>
        <p class="muted">Let’s get some answers</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" style="gap:14px">
        <p>Mis-selling isn’t just the feeling that you’ve paid too much — it’s about not getting the full picture. Below are a few quick questions to help you determine if you were mis-led when you agreed to your finance deal.</p>
        <ul>{QUESTIONS.map((q) => <li>{q}</li>)}</ul>
        <p class="small muted">{FREE_ROUTE}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
